  "reply_raw": "```json\n{\"mode\": \"precedent\", \"rule\": {\"action\": \"attach_role\", \"resource\": \"*\", \"conditions\": {\"incident_active\": [\"eq\", \"1\"], \"scope_match\": [\"eq\", \"1\"], \"role_tier\": [\"le\", \"1\"], \"ttl_min\": [\"le\", \"30\"], \"purpose\": [\"eq\", \"availability\"]}}}\n```\n\nThe 10 tasks were uniform: incident active, scope match confirmed, tier 1, availability purpose, TTL 15 or 30 minutes. A standing rule bounded by those confirmed facts covers the recurring case without widening scope. Role tier is capped at 1, TTL at 30 minutes, and both the incident flag and scope check must be set — so privileged grants outside an active, in-scope incident still require a case.",
